Lobium - apply the persona timezone inside the engine, not through the environment.

The launcher sets TZ/LANG/LC_ALL before spawning the browser, which is how the persona timezone
reaches ICU on Linux. On Windows that route does not exist: ICU reads the timezone from the registry
and ignores TZ entirely, so the profile's timezone silently did not apply at all - Date, Intl and
every timezone-derived value reported the HOST zone while the persona claimed another, which a page
compares against the proxy exit IP in one line of JavaScript.

Hook point: TimeZoneController::OnTimeZoneChange, deliberately.

An earlier attempt hooked RenderThreadImpl::Init to adopt the persona zone at renderer startup. That
does not survive: the browser's device::TimeZoneMonitor pushes the HOST zone to every renderer
shortly after start, overwriting whatever was adopted earlier. OnTimeZoneChange is the receiving end
of that push, so overriding there is applied both at startup and on every subsequent host change,
and no later notification can undo it.

The explicit override path (HasTimeZoneOverride, used by DevTools emulation) is left in control when
it is active: an operator emulating a zone in DevTools should see the zone they asked for.

Hook point: third_party/blink/renderer/core/timezone/timezone_controller.cc

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/timezone/timezone_controller.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/timezone/timezone_controller.cc
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/timezone/timezone_controller.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/timezone/timezone_controller.cc
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/timezone/timezone_controller.h"
 
 #include "base/feature_list.h"
+#include "components/lobium_fp/lobium_fp_config.h"
 #include "mojo/public/cpp/bindings/pending_remote.h"
 #include "mojo/public/cpp/bindings/remote.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/public/common/thread_safe_browser_interface_broker_proxy.h"
@@ -245,12 +246,36 @@ void TimeZoneController::OnTimeZoneChange(const String& timezone_id) {
 
   base::AutoLock locker(instance().lock_);
 
+  // Lobium: substitute the persona IANA zone for the host's.
+  //
+  // This is THE renderer-side authority for the ICU default zone, and hooking anywhere earlier does
+  // not work. The browser's device::TimeZoneMonitor pushes the host zone id to every renderer: once
+  // when TimeZoneController::Init() registers as a client during Blink startup (AddClient calls back
+  // immediately), and again on every host zone change. Any adoptDefault done before that - for
+  // instance alongside the ICU locale in RenderThreadImpl::Init - is simply overwritten by that
+  // push. On a sandboxed Windows renderer the in-renderer zone detection is blocked anyway, so ICU
+  // starts at UTC and the browser push is the only thing that ever sets it: exactly the observed
+  // "reports UTC while the persona says America/New_York" leak.
+  //
+  // Substituting here covers the main frame, iframes and dedicated/shared/service workers in one
+  // place, because SetIcuTimeZoneAndNotifyV8 calls icu::TimeZone::adoptDefault and then
+  // DateTimeConfigurationChangeNotification on the main isolate AND every worker thread - so both
+  // Intl.DateTimeFormat and Date observe it. Recording it as host_timezone_id_ additionally means
+  // that clearing a DevTools timezone override restores the PERSONA zone, not the host's.
+  //
+  // Fail open: an absent or empty configured timezone leaves the real host value untouched.
+  String effective_timezone_id = timezone_id;
+  if (const lobium::LobiumFpConfig* cfg = lobium::LobiumFpConfig::Current();
+      cfg && !cfg->locale.timezone.empty()) {
+    effective_timezone_id = String::FromUtf8(cfg->locale.timezone);
+  }
+
   // Remember requested timezone id so we can set it when timezone
   // override is removed.
-  instance().host_timezone_id_ = timezone_id;
+  instance().host_timezone_id_ = effective_timezone_id;
 
   if (!HasTimeZoneOverride())
-    SetIcuTimeZoneAndNotifyV8(timezone_id);
+    SetIcuTimeZoneAndNotifyV8(effective_timezone_id);
 }
 
